{0 Workspace validation, plans and journals}

{!Libtmux_workspace.Config} validates native descriptions without I/O.
{!Libtmux_workspace.Plan} combines configuration with an explicit observation.
A missing endpoint is distinct from an empty captured graph. Default collisions
fail; append requires an explicit new-window policy.

{1 Execute through a backend}

{!Libtmux_workspace.Execution} delegates I/O to an executor. Ordinary callers
use a backend's Workspace module, retain the handle before awaiting, then
inspect its immutable journal after cancellation or partial failure.

Plans belong to one connection generation and recheck their captured
preconditions before mutation. Preview output is advisory. Compensation removes
only resources proven newly created by that operation, in reverse order.
Unbound startup hints are not operational targets and cannot authorize cleanup.
